wmsystemtray
============

wmsystemtray is a freedesktop.org system tray for Window Maker. It supports
multiple dock windows and paging when more icons are active than can fit.
This source is version 1.4, written by Brad Jorsch and released under the
GNU General Public License, version 2 or later; see COPYING.

Build dependencies
------------------

- Meson 0.60 or newer and Ninja
- A C compiler and pkg-config
- X11, Xext, Xfixes, and Xpm development libraries

On Fedora, install the dependencies with:

    sudo dnf install gcc meson ninja-build pkgconf-pkg-config \
        libX11-devel libXext-devel libXfixes-devel libXpm-devel

Build and install
-----------------

From this directory:

    meson setup build
    meson compile -C build
    sudo meson install -C build

The executable is installed under the selected bindir (normally
/usr/local/bin), and the manual page is installed under the selected mandir.
To stage an install for packaging:

    meson setup build --prefix=/usr
    DESTDIR=/tmp/package-root meson install -C build

Run `wmsystemtray --help` for command-line options. See wmsystemtray(1) for
the complete usage documentation.

Meson is the maintained build system for this fork; the obsolete Autotools
build infrastructure from the original archive is not retained.
